    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d774">

                <pb facs="0865" n="579" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg579"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-01T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 1, 1917, 7 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4377. See Consul London’s despatch 3474, January 17. Unofficially inform Foreign
                    Office that your representations based on <pb facs="0866" n="580" xml:id="pg580"
                    /> Department’s 4330, January 24, as to permits for needles of German origin to
                    British houses is confirmed by statement of Procurator General and that under
                    circumstances Department feels justified in expecting prompt assurances of
                    non-interference with needles covered by Department’s instruction 4512,<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d774-f1"/> November 25.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
